{
  "packs": [
    "basics",
    "github-actions",
    {
      "id": "grow_with_claudinite",
      "config": {
        "pack_paths": [
          ".claudinite/local/packs",
          "packs"
        ]
      }
    },
    "tidy-repo",
    {
      "id": "local/claudinite",
      "config": {
        "canaryRepo": "missingbulb/ClaudiniteCanary"
      }
    },
    "local/canon-curation",
    {
      "id": "barriers",
      "answers": {
        "goals": "Keep extending.md's engine/content boundary structural: core (checks/, mount/, engine/, .github/, the top-level docs, and the shared engine modules under packs/ and skills/) must never name a specific pack or skill — packs and skills are discovered content, and a core file citing one couples the engine to its content. One rule per namespace (packs/*, skills/*); reviewed inherent couplings live in each rule's except. migrations/ is deliberately NOT core here: a migration record is a dated one-off that exists to move the fleet off a specific pack's old shape, so naming that pack is its purpose, not a coupling — and records accumulate as dated folders, one per change, which no path-keyed exception list should have to chase."
      },
      "config": {
        "rules": [
          {
            "from": [
              "engine",
              ".github",
              "bootstrap.md",
              "consumer-safe-changes.md",
              "extending.md"
            ],
            "to": "packs/*",
            "matchNames": true,
            "matchUniqueFilenames": false,
            "reason": "core is the engine that runs pack content — it must not name the specific packs it runs (extending.md)",
            "except": [
              {
                "path": ".github/workflows/README.md",
                "to": [
                  "packs/chrome-extension",
                  "packs/chrome-extension-release"
                ],
                "reason": "decouple(release-infra): the core .github/ README documents the chrome-extension-release plumbing being vendored out of core (#276)"
              },
              {
                "path": ".github/workflows/chrome-extension-daily-release.yml",
                "to": [
                  "packs/chrome-extension",
                  "packs/chrome-extension-release",
                  "packs/github-actions"
                ],
                "reason": "decouple(release-infra): chrome-extension-release reusable release infra hosted in the core .github/ tree; being vendored out (#276)"
              },
              {
                "path": ".github/workflows/chrome-extension-publish-store.yml",
                "to": [
                  "packs/chrome-extension",
                  "packs/chrome-extension-release"
                ],
                "reason": "decouple(release-infra): chrome-extension-release reusable release infra hosted in the core .github/ tree; being vendored out (#276)"
              },
              {
                "path": ".github/workflows/chrome-extension-release.yml",
                "to": [
                  "packs/chrome-extension",
                  "packs/chrome-extension-release"
                ],
                "reason": "decouple(release-infra): chrome-extension-release reusable release infra hosted in the core .github/ tree; being vendored out (#276)"
              },
              {
                "path": ".github/actions/read-release-config/read-config.mjs",
                "to": [
                  "packs/chrome-extension-release"
                ],
                "reason": "decouple(release-infra): a chrome-release composite action in the core .github/ tree; being vendored out (#276)"
              },
              {
                "path": "extending.md",
                "to": [
                  "packs/grow_with_claudinite"
                ],
                "reason": "inherent(#385): the engine map documents where the adoption-interview machinery lives now that it is bundled in the adoption skill"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "siblings": "packs",
            "to": "docs",
            "reason": "docs/ is outside the vendor set, so a pack file's reference to it resolves to nothing in every consumer (#424) — cite the doc from the issue or PR instead"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "claude-code-web-users-support",
      "config": {
        "repo": "missingbulb/Sheepdog"
      },
      "answers": {
        "store": "missingbulb/Sheepdog — the fleet's own repo, which holds one <email>.md per person under preferences/"
      }
    }
  ],
  "accept": [
    {
      "rule": "reference-integrity",
      "path": "docs/per-project-scheduling/",
      "reason": "the per-project-scheduling DESIGN/MIGRATION pair is the historical record of migration #394 — it names the central routine and planner files this migration deleted precisely because deleting them is what it records; rewriting those names would falsify the record, so its inbound-reference dangling is deliberate and permanent"
    },
    {
      "rule": "file-placement",
      "path": "engine/checks/helpers/repo-context.mjs",
      "reason": "the engine's file-set builder deliberately imports the consumer-layout constant SHARED_SUBDIR (beside LOCAL_PACKS_SUBDIR in engine/pack_loader/pack-registry.mjs — core machinery per extending.md, not a specific pack) so the shared-mount sweep exclusion and the vendor writer share one definition; the cross-tree reach is inherent, not a misplacement"
    },
    {
      "rule": "file-placement",
      "path": "engine/migrations/registry.mjs",
      "reason": "the canon-side migration registry deliberately builds on the vendored sync surface in the engine lib (engine/checks/helpers/active-migrations.mjs — the home pack-independence mandates, since pack checks consult migrationActive and packs import only the engine surface); one definition, re-exported for canon callers, so the cross-tree reach is inherent, not a misplacement"
    },
    {
      "rule": "file-placement",
      "path": "updates/",
      "reason": "an update flow is by definition the composition of the trees it moves between — the vendor-set computation it lays down, the engine surface it replaces, the migration registry it runs and the wiring it converges — so every import it has crosses a tree boundary; that reach IS the module, and putting it inside any one of those trees would either ship canon-internal machinery to every member or hide the flow inside the thing it operates on"
    },
    {
      "rule": "file-placement",
      "path": "packs/static-website/version-scheme.mjs",
      "reason": "the version rule deliberately imports the scheme itself (VERSION_RE, the version reader) and the config parser from the pack's own vendored stubs, because those files are the definition: they are what runs in every site repo's .github/. Restating either canon-side would be a second copy that drifts from the code that actually bumps and reads. The reach into stubs/ is inherent to a pack whose logic ships vendored, not a misplacement"
    },
    {
      "rule": "file-placement",
      "path": "packs/static-website/site-config.mjs",
      "reason": "same as version-scheme.mjs: the config rule parses .github/site.config with the very parser the vendored read-site-config action runs, so the check and the pipeline can never disagree about what a valid config is"
    },
    {
      "rule": "file-placement",
      "path": "packs/static-website/release-workflows.mjs",
      "reason": "same as site-config.mjs: the pipeline-completeness rule reads .github/site.config with the vendored parser to see whether the repo declares build_vars, because the answer decides whether a pre-exporter vendored copy is stale or simply untouched. Re-parsing the config canon-side would be a second definition of a valid config that drifts from the one the runner uses"
    },
    {
      "rule": "file-placement",
      "path": "vendoring/compute-vendor-set.mjs",
      "reason": "the vendor-set computation deliberately imports the import-surface facts from the engine lib (engine/checks/helpers/module-imports.mjs — the one home the pack-independence check judges against), so \"what a pack may import\" and \"what a vendor set must carry\" share one definition; the cross-tree reach is inherent, not a misplacement"
    },
    {
      "rule": "barrier",
      "path": ".github/workflows/canary-rehearsal.yml",
      "reason": "the live canary gate names packs/basics/tasks/update because the worker is ITSELF vendored content, so a release that changes the worker cannot be rehearsed by the canary's vendored copy — that copy predates the release by definition, and a rehearsal driving it would ignore CLAUDINITE_CANON_REF entirely and run a real cycle against main, opening a PR on the canary instead of qualifying the ref. The crossing buys the one property the gate exists for: the code under test is the code every member runs the moment the release reaches them. The workflow names no pack CONTENT — only the entry point of the task that performs the converge"
    }
  ],
  "taskScheduler": {
    "dailyHour": 4,
    "weeklyDay": "Sun",
    "monthlyDay": 1
  }
}

